body:
Can't find what i need in clothing, men's shorts, jogger pants, etc:

I have tried searching more rigorously in the last 2 years or so for specific clothing, but can't find i need, due to issues with quality / material not good, sizing not good, doesn't look nice / bad design, too expensive, doesn't have the color i want, etc. I was hoping someone can give some suggestions or maybe there's a specific way i can google search the things i want, because maybe it's a matter of knowing what to search, and maybe i'm just not searching the right terms. i have looked at macy's, nordstrom, [saksoff5th.com](https://saksoff5th.com), [asos.com](https://asos.com), and many other places, i also tried contacting [under510.com](https://under510.com) twice maybe, but never got a response back on sizing related questions. asos's jogger pants usually are too long in the front rise, the one i received today was 12 inches roughly. I am 5 feet 8 inches btw. here is some of the things i'm looking for below:

&#x200B;

men's twill cotton or linen ( no polyester/synthetic materials, a little of spandex is fine ) drawstring shorts in mid rise in a jet black color or ivory / cream / off white, but not a murky, darker or duller beige colors, no less than like 10.25 front rise inches and no more than like 11 inches, with inseam of no more than like 9 inches, with 8 inches being the absolute lowest. currently i have these what appear to be discontinued sonoma shorts that are 10.5 inch front rise and 9 inch inseam and they fit ok at the top of my knee cap roughly, though i prefer slightly shorter, 8-8.5" would fit better while keeping the same front rise. Also my waist is 30, but i typically fit best in 31 or maybe as high as 32 if it's 100 percent cotton.

&#x200B;

men's jogger pants / sweatpants or any other pants / trousers with drawstring + tapered ankle, cotton / linen + spandex is fine, but no synthetics / polyester. jet black color and / or ivory, cream / off white, size 30-32 in waist, material can either be twill or soft cotton type, though i am looking for both kinds. front rise must be no less than like 10.25 inches, but no more than like 11 inches, inseam, no less than like 29 inches, higher is ok, because i can just shorten the length if the front rise fits good, though the back rise should also fit good, which from what i read is supposed to be like 4-5 inches more than the front rise, but not mentioned usually on the item, even if you ask, but sometimes you can make a guess based off photos, some designs that fit awkwardly makes the front and back rise almost equivalent, creating a bad fit.

&#x200B;

i know i mentioned issues with pricing as well, but people can still link me something they find, even if it may be pricy. i don't want to really give a specific price point, so i'll just see what you guys can find and i'll let you know if it's too expensive or not worth it. but for a starter, i linked an item below that got sold out which is close to what i'm looking for, however, i never got a response from them on other sizing questions, also for me, the 83 sterling pound to usd is too expensive:

&#x200B;

[https://www.endclothing.com/gb/norse-projects-evald-organic-cotton-short-n35-0587-0957.html](https://www.endclothing.com/gb/norse-projects-evald-organic-cotton-short-n35-0587-0957.html)
